title: AI4RA Unified Data Model (UDM)
message: >-
  If you use this work, in whole or in part, please cite it as below.
  Attribution is required by the license (CC BY 4.0 for the standard,
  Apache-2.0 for the code). NOTICE lists which files fall under which
  license and the attribution each requires.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Layman
    given-names: Nathan
    affiliation: University of Idaho
repository-code: https://github.com/ui-insight/AI4RA-UDM
url: https://ui-insight.github.io/AI4RA-UDM/
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: https://ui-insight.github.io/AI4RA-UDM/data/udm_schema.json
    description: Canonical machine-readable schema (current version)
abstract: >-
  A canonical schema for research administration covering pre-award
  proposal preparation, sponsor submission, post-award management,
  financial accounting, personnel effort, compliance, and operational
  systems. The UDM is a specification. Institutions implement it in
  whatever database technology fits their environment, and it is
  published as machine-readable JSON to support direct integration, ERD
  generation, and schema-aware tooling.
keywords:
  - research administration
  - data model
  - schema
  - grants management
  - pre-award
  - post-award
  - medallion architecture
  - lakehouse
